      "role": "user",
      "content": "yo i keep getting an 'Access Denied' error when my lambda trying to write logs to s3 even though i think the policy is right. can u look at this?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It looks like your IAM policy allows putting objects to the specified S3 bucket, but you also need to allow `s3:PutObjectTagging` for Lambda to create and write logs. Here's what you should add to your policy:\n\n```json\n\"PutObjectTagging\": \"s3:PutObjectTagging\"\n```\n\nThis should resolve the 'Access Denied' error when your Lambda function tries to write logs to the S3 bucket. Make sure to update your policy and then test again.",
